#### scenario E: DefWindowProc(WM_ERASEBKGND) with a memory DC
E1 solid brush (class csolid)
  E WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  whole DC: result=1 pixels (0,0)=563412 (8,8)=563412 (15,15)=563412
  E WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  clip (4,4,10,8): result=1 pixels (5,5)=563412 (4,4)=563412 (9,7)=563412 (10,7)=404040 (3,5)=404040 (12,6)=404040 (5,8)=404040
E2 no brush (class cnone)
  E WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 0
  whole DC: result=0 pixels (0,0)=404040 (8,8)=404040 (15,15)=404040
  E WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 0
  clip (4,4,10,8): result=0 pixels (5,5)=404040 (4,4)=404040 (9,7)=404040 (10,7)=404040 (3,5)=404040 (12,6)=404040 (5,8)=404040
E3 COLOR_WINDOW + 1 (class cwin)
  E WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  whole DC: result=1 pixels (0,0)=ffffff (8,8)=ffffff (15,15)=ffffff
  E WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  clip (4,4,10,8): result=1 pixels (5,5)=ffffff (4,4)=ffffff (9,7)=ffffff (10,7)=404040 (3,5)=404040 (12,6)=404040 (5,8)=404040
E4 CS_PARENTDC with a brush (class cpar)
  E WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  whole DC: result=1 pixels (0,0)=563412 (8,8)=563412 (15,15)=563412
  E WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  clip (4,4,10,8): result=1 pixels (5,5)=563412 (4,4)=563412 (9,7)=563412 (10,7)=404040 (3,5)=404040 (12,6)=404040 (5,8)=404040
#### scenario P: the erase of a window DC
P1 default WM_PAINT, class with a brush (window WS, class csolid)
  WS WM_PAINT (default)
  WS WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P2 default WM_PAINT, class without a brush (window WN, class cnone)
  WN WM_PAINT (default)
  WN WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 0
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P3 own BeginPaint, class with a brush (window C1, class csolid)
  C1 WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  C1 WM_PAINT BeginPaint fErase=0 rcPaint=(10,10,50,40)
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P4 own BeginPaint, class without a brush (window C2, class cnone)
  C2 WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 0
  C2 WM_PAINT BeginPaint fErase=1 rcPaint=(10,10,50,40)
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P5 own BeginPaint, bErase FALSE (window C3, class csolid)
  C3 WM_PAINT BeginPaint fErase=0 rcPaint=(10,10,50,40)
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P6 RDW_ERASENOW then BeginPaint, class with a brush (window C4, class csolid)
  C4 WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  after RDW_ERASENOW: update rect 1 (10,10,50,40)
  C4 WM_PAINT BeginPaint fErase=0 rcPaint=(10,10,50,40)
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P7 RDW_ERASENOW then BeginPaint, class without a brush (window C5, class cnone)
  C5 WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 0
  after RDW_ERASENOW: update rect 1 (10,10,50,40)
  C5 WM_PAINT BeginPaint fErase=1 rcPaint=(10,10,50,40)
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P8 the DC of WM_ERASEBKGND is clipped to the update region (BeginPaint) (window Q1, class csolid)
  Q1 WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 probe(inside the update rect)=1 probe(outside)=0 -> 1
  Q1 WM_PAINT BeginPaint fErase=0 rcPaint=(10,10,50,40)
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P9 the DC of WM_ERASEBKGND is clipped to the update region (RDW_ERASENOW) (window Q2, class csolid)
  Q2 WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 probe(inside the update rect)=1 probe(outside)=0 -> 1
  after RDW_ERASENOW: update rect 1 (10,10,50,40)
  Q2 WM_PAINT BeginPaint fErase=0 rcPaint=(10,10,50,40)
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
P10 the DC of WM_ERASEBKGND is clipped to the update region (default WM_PAINT) (window Q3, class csolid)
  Q3 WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 probe(inside the update rect)=1 probe(outside)=0 -> 1
  Q3 WM_PAINT BeginPaint fErase=0 rcPaint=(10,10,50,40)
  after: update rect 0 (0,0,0,0)
#### scenario T: WM_NCHITTEST answered HTTRANSPARENT
T1 two top-level pop-ups of one thread, the upper one (TB) transparent: a click where they overlap goes to the one beneath (A):
 click (160,120): in both:
  TB WM_NCHITTEST
  TB WM_NCHITTEST
  TB WM_NCHITTEST
 click (280,200): only in TB: nothing beneath:
  TB WM_NCHITTEST
  TB WM_NCHITTEST
  TB WM_NCHITTEST
 click (60,50): only in A:
  A WM_NCHITTEST
  A WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  A WM_MOUSEMOVE x=40 y=30
  A WM_NCHITTEST
  A WM_MOUSEACTIVATE hit=1 msg=0x201
  A WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x201
  A WM_LBUTTONDOWN x=40 y=30
  A WM_NCHITTEST
  A WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  A WM_LBUTTONUP x=40 y=30
  A WM_NCHITTEST
T2 a transparent child (TC) of a pop-up (P): the click goes to P:
 click (80,80): in TC:
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  P WM_MOUSEMOVE x=40 y=40
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x201
  P WM_LBUTTONDOWN x=40 y=40
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  P WM_LBUTTONUP x=40 y=40
  P WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
T3 an opaque child (C) of a pop-up (P) over a transparent child (TC): C is above TC and takes the click; a click on TC alone goes to P:
 click (160,120): in C (and in TC):
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  C WM_NCHITTEST
  C WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  C WM_MOUSEMOVE x=20 y=20
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  C WM_NCHITTEST
  C WM_MOUSEACTIVATE hit=1 msg=0x201
  P WM_MOUSEACTIVATE hit=1 msg=0x201
  C WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x201
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x201
  C WM_LBUTTONDOWN x=20 y=20
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  C WM_NCHITTEST
  C WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  C WM_LBUTTONUP x=20 y=20
 click (80,80): in TC only:
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  P WM_MOUSEMOVE x=40 y=40
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x201
  P WM_LBUTTONDOWN x=40 y=40
  TC WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  P WM_LBUTTONUP x=40 y=40
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
  P WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
T4 (not part of the HTTRANSPARENT change; S-disabled-drops of decision 0136) a disabled child (D) of a pop-up (P): Wine 10.0 skips a disabled child, so P gets the click; the runtime drops it:
 click (80,80): in D:
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  P WM_MOUSEMOVE x=40 y=40
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x201
  P WM_LBUTTONDOWN x=40 y=40
  P WM_NCHITTEST
  P WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  P WM_LBUTTONUP x=40 y=40
  P WM_ERASEBKGND dc=1 -> 1
T5 (same) a disabled top-level pop-up (DP): Wine 10.0 answers the hit with HTERROR and sends WM_SETCURSOR to it; the runtime drops the event:
 click (100,80): in DP:
  DP WM_SETCURSOR hit=-2 msg=0x200
  DP WM_SETCURSOR hit=-2 msg=0x201
  DP WM_SETCURSOR hit=-2 msg=0x202
#### scenario H: WH_MOUSE and WH_KEYBOARD
H1 click on W with a mouse hook that lets everything pass:
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  HOOK0 mouse nCode=0 msg=0x200 pt=(100,80) hwnd=W ht=1
  HOOK0 -> 0
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  W WM_MOUSEMOVE x=70 y=50
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  HOOK0 mouse nCode=0 msg=0x201 pt=(100,80) hwnd=W ht=1
  HOOK0 -> 0
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x201
  W WM_LBUTTONDOWN x=70 y=50
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  HOOK0 mouse nCode=0 msg=0x202 pt=(100,80) hwnd=W ht=1
  HOOK0 -> 0
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  W WM_LBUTTONUP x=70 y=50
H2 the key A down and up with a keyboard hook that lets everything pass:
  HOOK2 key nCode=0 vk=0x41 lp=0x1e0001
  HOOK2 -> 0
  W WM_KEYDOWN vk=0x41 lp=0x1e0001
  HOOK2 key nCode=0 vk=0x41 lp=0xc01e0001
  HOOK2 -> 0
  W WM_KEYUP vk=0x41 lp=0xc01e0001
H3 the mouse hook answers 1 for WM_LBUTTONDOWN: W does not get it:
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  HOOK0 mouse nCode=0 msg=0x200 pt=(100,80) hwnd=W ht=1
  HOOK0 -> 0
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  W WM_MOUSEMOVE x=70 y=50
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  HOOK0 mouse nCode=0 msg=0x201 pt=(100,80) hwnd=W ht=1
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  HOOK0 mouse nCode=0 msg=0x202 pt=(100,80) hwnd=W ht=1
  HOOK0 -> 0
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  W WM_LBUTTONUP x=70 y=50
H4 the keyboard hook answers 1 for VK_A: W does not get the key down or up:
  HOOK2 key nCode=0 vk=0x41 lp=0x1e0001
  HOOK2 key nCode=0 vk=0x41 lp=0xc01e0001
H5 PeekMessage with PM_NOREMOVE (HC_NOREMOVE), then with PM_REMOVE (HC_ACTION):
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  HOOK0 mouse nCode=3 msg=0x200 pt=(120,90) hwnd=W ht=1
  HOOK0 -> 0
  peek(noremove) -> 0x200
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  HOOK0 mouse nCode=0 msg=0x200 pt=(120,90) hwnd=W ht=1
  HOOK0 -> 0
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  W WM_MOUSEMOVE x=90 y=60
  peek(remove) -> 0x200
H6 the mouse hook is removed: no hook line:
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x200
  W WM_MOUSEMOVE x=70 y=50
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x201
  W WM_LBUTTONDOWN x=70 y=50
  W WM_NCHITTEST
  W WM_SETCURSOR hit=1 msg=0x202
  W WM_LBUTTONUP x=70 y=50
